      "writtenOn": "2026-09-09T12:37:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`maglev-len` accepts 0, 1, and composite values, although Maglev requires a prime length greater than one. `cnat_translation_init_maglev()` divides by both `maglev_len` and `maglev_len - 1`, so 0/1 can crash VPP; a composite length can prevent table construction from completing. Could we validate this in `cnat_config()` and reject invalid values at startup?",
      "revId": "54c90ee95be3f38514e093d19b3b0e3f62777967",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
